// ar/hiking/index.astro — Arabic hiking hub pillar (AR-2 Phase F batch 6a, resumed).
// Mirrors src/pages/hiking/index.astro. SHAPE B — prose inline in the template, no
// page-content module and no content-collection read on the page itself. The surface was
// fully characterized on `guides`; nothing here re-derives it.
//
// ⚠ ONE ELEMENT SHAPE B HAD NOT YET SHOWN: the offscreen `<p class="page-summary">`. It is
// positioned off-canvas but `aria-hidden="false"`, so it RENDERS and every bidi contract
// applies to it exactly as to visible prose — the phone inside it is isolated, not bare.
// The JSON-LD copies of the same number stay bare: isolate what renders, never what is parsed.
//
// SLOT 1 — no probe run. Every digit-bearing construct on this page falls in an already
// measured class, and the authoring resolutions are the established ones:
//   13,528 / 5,331 / 13,000 / 200   comma-grouped or bare magnitude, measured LTR -> bare
//   ~20 min / ~1 hour               leading marker (7c) -> the marker becomes the word `نحو`
//   30–90 / 30–90+ / 10–11          en-dash range, measured reversing -> spelled `من … إلى …`
//   (435) 219-9447                  digit-separator-digit + brackets -> <bdi>
//   $349                            measured reversing -> the established `349 دولارًا`
//
// §2.2 — first contact for `Green River`, `Yampa`, `Split Mountain`, `Kings Peak`,
// `Little Hole`, `Harpers Corner`, `Josie Morris`, `Uinta Highline Trail`, `Navajo`. All stay
// Latin, following the corpus's existing `Flaming Gorge` / `Red Fleet` / `Uinta` treatment.
// Per batch 4, every one was checked for a §3.6 shape: none carries a digit separator.
// States are localised (`يوتا`), matching `كولورادو` / `وايومنغ` already in the corpus.
//
// §3.5 — two parentheticals in the English would have closed on a Latin run once translated
// (`~20 min east (Quarry area)`, the figcaption's `Kings Peak (13,528 ft)`); both are rewritten
// to an em dash and an apposition rather than bracketed.
//
// §4 — 15 of the 17 internal targets are registered `ar` routes and switch. `/camping/` and
// `/scenic-drives/` stay English; both land in batch 6b.
